#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_exists

#% text
# `key_exists(a, k)` gives `true` when the association `a` has the key `k`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_exists(assoc("x" -> 1), "x")
#% output
#= true

#% cell
key_exists(assoc("x" -> 1), "y")
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Looking up a missing key gives a `missing_key` failure; test with `key_exists` first:

#% cell
assoc("x" -> 1)["y"]
#% output
#! failure(missing_key, "y")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `lookup`, `keys`, `insert`
